From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:05:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/33] media: i2c: add Sony IMX766 image sensor driver

Add a V4L2 sub-device driver for the Sony IMX766 with one binned
4096x3072 RAW10 mode at 30 fps over three MIPI CSI-2 C-PHY trios from a
24 MHz INCK, using the CCI register helpers. It exposes exposure,
analogue and digital gain, vertical blanking, flips and the sensor test
patterns, and does not change the INCK rate.

The register settings come from the MediaTek imgsensor imx766 driver.
---
 MAINTAINERS                |   8 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Kconfig  |  10 +
 drivers/media/i2c/Makefile |   1 +
 drivers/media/i2c/imx766.c | 962 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 981 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/i2c/imx766.c

